// bootstrap.lz — Luazi 64-bit Self-Hosting Compiler Bootstrap
// Main entry point that progressively builds the compiler in Luazi itself.
//
// 64-bit Architecture:
//   - Instructions: 64-bit (8 bytes)
//   - Registers: 64-bit wide, 16-bit indexable (up to 65,536 registers)
//   - Constants: 40-bit index (up to ~1 trillion constants)
//   - Memory: 64-bit addressing
//   - Numbers: IEEE 754 double-precision (f64)
//
// Usage:
//   luazi bootstrap.lz                    # Run bootstrap
//   luazi bootstrap.lz --compile <file>   # Compile a .lz file
//   luazi bootstrap.lz --run <file>       # Run a .lz file
//   luazi bootstrap.lz --repl             # Start REPL
//   luazi bootstrap.lz --check <file>     # Type-check only
//   luazi bootstrap.lz --test             # Run bootstrap tests

// ============================================================================
// IMPORTS — Self-hosted compiler modules (64-bit)
// ============================================================================

